Scripts and commands used to cluster virus-like genomes into vOTUs.

Step 1: Run blastn of open reading frame (orf) sequences in genomes against each other.

Step 1a: Make blast database
Required files: open reading frame sequences
makeblastdb -in test_data/test_viruslike_orfs.fna -dbtype nucl -parse_seqids -out test_viruslike_orf_blastdb/test_viruslike_orf_blastdb

Step 1b: Run blastn search of orf sequences against orf database with a max Evalue ov 10-5 and output in tab-delimited format 6
blastn  -db  test_viruslike_orf_blastdb/test_viruslike_orf_blastdb -query test_data/test_viruslike_orfs.fna -out test_viruslike_orf_blastn.txt -outfmt=6 -evalue 0.00001

Step 2: Parse blastn output table to calculate ANI between genomes and filter for thos with >= 95% across >= 85% coding sequence length (total orf length).
vOTUs are determined by single linkage clustering with these thresholds. Each genome is assigned a vOTU based on this clustering. Singletons receive a vOTU name as well "vOTU_[insert number]" because self-hits are retained.
Required files: (1) blast output from step 1b (e.g. test_data/test_viruslike_orf_blastn.txt), (2) tab-seperated table with each open reading frame's lengths formatted as specified in example (e.g. test_data/test_orf_lens.tsv)
python 0_calc_votu.py -i test_data/test_viruslike_orf_blastn.txt -l test_data/test_orf_lens.tsv -n test_data/test

Output table: test_data/test_votu_membership.tsv contains first column with genome name and second column with vOTU name
